<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Travel hydration principles">
  <div><strong>Plan access</strong><span>Carry a refillable bottle and identify safe water after security and at the destination.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Cabins are dry</strong><span>Low humidity can increase water loss, but healthy travelers do not need extreme fluid intake.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Movement is separate</strong><span>Hydration does not replace walking or individualized thrombosis precautions on long trips.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__feature">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Travel reality</p>
    <h2>Disrupted routine is usually the bigger issue</h2>
    <p>Security, unfamiliar refill points, long sitting periods and changed meal or sleep timing can make normal drinking less convenient. Aircraft cabins are also dry, but there is no need to force excessive fluid simply because you are flying.</p>
    <p>A practical routine is to begin normally hydrated, refill after security when possible and drink regularly with meals and activity.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Travel kit</p>
  <h2>Keep it portable</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4">
    <article><h3>Reusable bottle</h3><p>Carry it empty through security where permitted, then refill.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Dry powder</h3><p>Keep Best Hydrate sealed until safe water is available, then mix according to the label.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Safe water</h3><p>When local water safety is uncertain, follow public-health guidance and use treated or sealed water.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Keep moving</h3><p>Movement during long travel serves a different purpose from hydration. Higher-risk travelers should seek individualized advice.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Where Best Hydrate may fit</p>
    <h2>A familiar drink when the routine changes</h2>
    <p>Powder is easy to carry and mix later with safe water. Best Hydrate can fit long travel days, hot destinations or activity after arrival.</p>
    <p>It should not be presented as protection against blood clots, altitude illness, jet lag or travel-associated disease.</p>
